Based on the context documents provided, when a streaming resume attempt fails with HTTP 409 (checkpoint mismatch), the server's error payload includes the following JSON schema:

```json
{
  "title": "Streaming Resume Error Payload",
  "type": "object",
  "properties": {
    "error": {
      "type": "object",
      "properties": {
        "code": {
          "type": "integer",
          "minimum": 409
        },
        "message": {
          "type": "string",
          "minLength": 1
        },
        "details": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "resume_version": {
              "type": "integer"
            },
            "resume_details": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "checkpoint_seq": {
                  "type": "integer"
                },
                "resume_seq": {
                  "type": "integer"
                },
                "resume_offset": {
                  "type": "integer"
                },
                "resume_watermark": {
                  "type": "integer"
                },
                "resume_crc": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "hex"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

